{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Root cause CONFIRMED on current main (worktree bluebottle2-gitretry, branched from origin/main).\n\nRead the retry family in src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:\n- run_git_write composes _with_index_lock_retry (OUTER, git lock signatures) around _with_transient_head_retry (INNER).\n- _with_transient_head_retry matches only _is_transient_head_error, whose marker sets are _TRANSIENT_HEAD_MARKERS = ('could not parse head',) and _TRANSIENT_OBJECT_MARKERS = ('bad object',). Both are READ-side signatures (HEAD parse, parse_object returning NULL).\n- Neither substring matches git's write-side loose-object temp-create fault ('unable to create temporary file' / 'failed to insert into database' / 'unable to index file'), so run_git_write returns that failure on its first attempt.\n\nConfirmed the asymmetric counterpart: src/rebar/_store/event_append.py defines _TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS with exactly those three write-side markers, wrapped by _with_transient_add_retry, and composes it ONLY into event_append's own _git_add / _git_commit / _git_commit_paths and the two recovery commits. Grep over src confirms no other module references that family, so every non-event_append caller of the shared seam (s3_doctor, which imports run_git_write and is_transient_object_read_error; compaction; the claim/transition writers) is unprotected against the write-side fault class.\n\nSo the asymmetry the bug describes is real and present: the identical runner-FS fault self-heals on the git add path and hard-fails on the shared write seam. Proceeding to fix by moving the write-side marker family into gitutil so there is ONE definition and every run_git_write caller inherits the bounded retry."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786603763718337001,"uuid":"3323a761-045e-4171-8c2a-29c400eb7e8f"}